{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["Its lamps — 'lucernae' in the vernacular, into which one puts the oil and the wicks." "And he shall light — the priest." "Its lamps — seven upon the seven branches." "And it shall give light over the face of it — he kindles the wicks toward the side facing the menorah, which is toward the table opposite it, as written: ואת המנורה נוכח השלחן. And so it says: אל מול פני המנורה יאירו שבעת הנרות — that all seven of them give light toward the table opposite it, to its face."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "Old French לוצי\"ש renders as 'lucernae' (lamps/lampholders), following the standard identification of this gloss."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:43:06.869265059Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}